<%= render "views/_header.ecr" %>

<nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <a href="/">Snippets</a>
  <span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span>
  <span>About</span>
</nav>

<article class="about-page">
  <h1 class="page-title">About Sage</h1>

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>What is Sage?</h2>
    <p>
      Sage is a lightweight, developer-focused code snippet manager and pastebin.
      It lets you save, browse, and search code snippets by programming language,
      with syntax highlighting for dozens of languages.
    </p>
    <p>
      Built for developers who want a fast, self-contained tool without accounts,
      sign-ups, or external services. Every snippet is public and instantly searchable.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>Features</h2>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li>Create snippets with a title, language tag, and code content</li>
      <li>Browse recent snippets on the homepage</li>
      <li>View any snippet with full syntax highlighting</li>
      <li>Search snippets by programming language</li>
      <li>Copy code to clipboard with one click</li>
      <li>Toggle between light and dark themes</li>
      <li>Fully responsive &mdash; works on mobile, tablet, and desktop</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>Technology</h2>
    <p>
      Sage is built with <strong>Crystal</strong> using the
      <strong>Kemal</strong> web framework, with <strong>SQLite</strong> for
      persistence and <strong>highlight.js</strong> for syntax highlighting.
      Server-rendered HTML with vanilla JavaScript keeps pages fast and lean.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>Supported Languages</h2>
    <div class="lang-list">
      <% %w[bash c crystal css dockerfile elixir go html java javascript json kotlin lua markdown php python ruby rust sql swift typescript yaml].each do |lang| %>
        <span class="badge badge-lang"><%= lang %></span>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>
</article>

<%= render "views/_footer.ecr" %>
